MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A claim returning ok:true does not prove lease ownership — a same-key duplicate
replay also returns ok:true — so a worker must verify before mutating a claimed
issue. Add `forge issue owns <id>`: a kernel-only READ that exits 0 iff the
resolving actor (FORGE_ACTOR -> FORGE_SESSION_ID -> default forge) holds the
single active claim AND the lease has not expired; otherwise it exits non-zero
(conflict, code 4) with a clear "you do not own the lease" message. Add the
reusable `claim-safety` skill (claim -> owns -> work -> re-verify before
close/release), registered in the kernel umbrella skill and mirrored to
.codex/skills. Regenerate the D20 bd call-site kill-list (line-shift only).

Closes eea2f9ce

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
